{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"41d2e4e84626e94887e6c7459781416f4ac2437d5bf651703cf286cb98669003","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion-verifier close gate and verdict persistence","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reconcile_verdict","_completion_precheck","completion_verifier_fail_v1","plan_review_result_v1","code_review_result_v1","plan_review/sidecar.py:157","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py",".rebar/run_snapshots/","ticket store sidecar"],"problem_keywords":["completion-verifier","fail verdict","durability","observability","calibration","audit trail","sidecar persistence"],"propositions":["FAILed completion-verifier verdicts currently vanish and are not persisted durably, making calibration audits impossible to reconstruct from system state alone.","A completion-verifier FAIL must be persisted as a reducer-ignored sidecar event in the ticket store (mirroring plan-review REVIEW_RESULT pattern) with schema version 'completion_verifier_fail_v1' before the FAIL verdict is raised in the close path.","The persisted FAIL record must include the failing criterion, findings array with remediation text per finding, model/runner identifier, timestamp, and ticket material fingerprint, making verdicts queryable offline.","Persistence failure must not alter the close path's behavior: the FAIL verdict must block the close and be raised unchanged, with the persistence error caught and swallowed in a best-effort try/except block.","Test coverage must validate both the happy path (FAIL verdict persisted with all required fields) and the failure path (persistence error does not mask or alter the FAIL verdict)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785818556369848125,"uuid":"94d8448e-dfc0-44b5-9def-2e177d979099"}